' @guidance:
' Create or update a HIGH-LEVEL PlantUML diagram describing how files containing
' @guidance tags are processed. Keep it big-picture: show only the main stages,
' not the detailed internal branching (see guidance-tag-processing.puml for detail).
'
' - This is a SEPARATE way of using Ghostwriter, NOT part of the Act functionality.
' - Show the essential pipeline: discover files -> extract guidance from the
'   @guidance: marker -> compose prompt -> dispatch to the GenAI provider -> report.
' - Prefer a small number of clear stages over exhaustive decision nodes.

@startuml
title Ghostwriter - @guidance Tag Processing (high-level overview)

skinparam ArrowColor #333333
skinparam ActivityBackgroundColor #F5F7FA
skinparam ActivityBorderColor #4A6FA5
skinparam ActivityDiamondBackgroundColor #FFF3CD
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #EDF7ED
skinparam PartitionBorderColor #999999

start

:Scan the project for candidate files
(reuses the standard project traversal);

:Extract guidance from each file
- find the "@guidance:" marker
- keep the marker in place;

if (Guidance present?) then (yes)
  :Use the file's inline guidance;
else (no)
  :Fall back to the default prompt
  (skip if none);
endif

:Compose the prompt
(instructions + rules + guidance);

:Dispatch to the GenAI provider
and apply file changes;

:Record the outcome in the report;

stop

@enduml
